.TH REMOLO 1 "2026" "remolo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
remolo \- reach a shell, files and the screen of another machine with one token
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B remolo
.I command
[options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
remolo runs in two roles from one binary. Start a host, copy the token it
prints, and from another machine run
.B remolo connect <token>
to land in a real shell. Endpoint discovery, encrypted transport selection and
authentication arrange themselves, including across NAT.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B host
Start a host and print a shareable session token. Options:
.B \-\-bind\fR,
.B \-\-ttl\fR,
.B \-\-loopback\fR,
.B \-\-once\fR,
.B \-\-identity \fIpath\fR (persistent host key),
.B \-\-mdns\fR,
.B \-\-stun\fR,
.B \-\-rendezvous\fR,
.B \-\-relay\fR,
.B \-\-file-root\fR,
.B \-\-cap \fIkind\fR,
.B \-\-cmd \fIname\fR,
.B \-\-ro\fR (least-privilege scoping).
.TP
.B connect \fItoken|alias\fR
Open an interactive remote shell. Ladder options:
.B \-\-mdns\fR,
.B \-\-rendezvous\fR,
.B \-\-relay\fR,
.B \-\-ssh-addr/-user/-key/-target\fR.
.B \-\-record \fIfile.cast\fR records the session (asciinema v2).
.TP
.B exec \fItoken|@group\fR [\-\-cwd \fIdir\fR] [\-\-env K=V] [\-\-env-pass K] [\-t] -- \fIcmd...\fR
Run a one-shot command. Exit code and stderr are propagated. @group fans out
over a host group in parallel.
.TP
.B desktop \fItoken\fR
Open a live interactive remote desktop in the browser (video plus mouse and
keyboard).
.TP
.B snapshot \fItoken\fR [\-\-num N]
Capture N screenshots of the host screen as PNG files.
.TP
.B put \fItoken local remote\fR, \fBget\fR \fItoken remote local\fR
Resumable, sha256-verified file transfer.
.TP
.B sync \fItoken local remote\fR [\-\-pull] [\-\-delete] [\-\-dry-run]
Incremental (rsync-like) directory sync.
.TP
.B forward \fItoken\fR [\-L \fIlport:host:rport\fR] [\-D \fIsocksport\fR]
Port forwarding over the remolo connection.
.TP
.B fs \fItoken\fR
Interactive remote file browser (ls, cd, get, put).
.TP
.B mount \fItoken mountpoint\fR
Mount the host filesystem locally via FUSE.
.TP
.B webterm \fItoken\fR
Serve a browser terminal (xterm.js) driving the remote shell.
.TP
.B rest \fItoken\fR \-\-addr \fIhost:port\fR
Expose a local REST API proxying to the host over RPC.
.TP
.B enroll \fItoken\fR \-\-as \fIname\fR, \fBrevoke\fR \fIfingerprint\fR
Register this client's key with the host so later connections need no token;
revoke runs on the host.
.TP
.B service install\fR, \fBservice uninstall\fR
Install or remove the host as a per-user background service.
.TP
.B info \fItoken\fR [\-\-json], \fBsessions\fR [\-\-json], \fBmux\fR, \fBalias\fR, \fBgroup\fR, \fBtoken\fR
Inspection and configuration.
.SH SECURITY
Sessions are end-to-end encrypted (TLS 1.3). The host is authenticated by
pinning its key from the token; the client by a pre-shared key (or an enrolled
client key). The token is the credential: treat it like a password. See
.B docs/security.md\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/remolo/config.json
Aliases, groups and defaults.
.TP
.B ~/.config/remolo/known_hosts
Remembered host keys (anti-swap protection).
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation at https://github.com/mirkobrombin/remolo
